WEBVTT

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:11.940
Your customers don't all talk the same way. Some chat, some email, and somebody has to answer all of them every day.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:20.380
Miss one, and that customer books somewhere else. The channels multiply, the team stays the same size, and the queue never clears.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.620
The gap isn't your service. It's the wiring between channels.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:30.980
Worry not, I'm here to close your loop. Here's what happens now. Every channel lands in one place.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:38.300
Telegram, WhatsApp, website chat, email, SMS. One AI brain answers them all on whatever model you prefer.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.140
It remembers each customer across channels, so nobody repeats themselves.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.620
It checks your real calendar and offers two real slots. It only books after the customer confirms.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:56.700
Emergencies and upset customers get escalated to a human every time. Every conversation lands in one log.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.860
Shared with your voice receptionist. New channels are a know-the-way, not a rebuild. One brain, every channel.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:10.620
If your channels are leaking customers, let's close that loop. Book a discovery call or send me an email.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.860
I'm Christian, n8n automation architect. Talk to you soon.
